# Godot runtime errors

On-screen script-error dialogs are dismissed by the user and are not visible to the agent.

**Always check** these files in the project root when debugging a play session:

1. `logs/godot_runtime.log` — script/engine errors via the `AgentLog` autoload (`SCRIPT` / `ERROR` / `WARNING` / `SHADER`). Prefer this for debugger popups.
2. `logs/godot_engine.log` — full Godot `--log-file` output from `start.bat` (stdout/stderr).

`godot_runtime.log` is truncated at each launch (session header), then appended. If it is missing, the game did not reach autoloads or was not run from this project — ask the user to relaunch (ideally via `start.bat`) and re-check.
